substantially stronger, but I land around **Alabama -17**. The revenge narrative from last year belongs in Don Delta, not baseline. The lightning delay adds another uncertainty input. citeturn419078news48turn446673news12\n- **Utah State +27.5 at Utah** is basically a pass for me. Utah deserves a monster number. Utah State playing Washington 16-14 gives me just enough resistance to land around **Utah -26.5**, but there is not enough separation from market to make it interesting. citeturn148717search1turn419078search4\n\nThe bigger methodology finding is already useful: **expected winner and spread value have to be separate fields.** In four of these five games, I still think the favorite is the more likely winner; the schema is asking whether the market has priced the winning margin correctly.\n\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT  \nCONFIDENCE: 87% structural / materially lower on exact fair-line precision  \nREASON: The five-game batch produced distinct and comparable model states without forcing one generic NCAA logic onto every matchup.  \nNEXT GATE: Let these games play → preserve the pregame artifact → postgame reconciliation against what actually drove the results  \nDON INPUT NEEDED: Yes — your reads on any of these before we see the outcomes are now clean prospective Don Evidence.", "text_chars": 2856, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["mnt/data/EC8_NCAA_1230_Pacific_Schema_Use_Case_2026-09-19.docx"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "edfbf5ae-705a-42ce-9f20-650fb7d6eb8c", "role": "tool", "role_name": "container.open_image", "created_at": 1789846595.8810759, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "execution_output", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has