hitecture, is:\n\n**FACT / GIVEN:** UNC entered 2–0 under Bill Belichick. Clemson entered 1–1, had major offensive problems, and was dealing with quarterback uncertainty. The market had already moved hard: Clemson opened around **-9.5** in some places and was down to roughly **-3.5** by kickoff. citeturn860883news5turn860883news1\n\n**DON EVIDENCE:** You were not buying Clemson’s historical brand value. Your read was that their current football state was materially worse than the name on the jersey suggested, while UNC had not yet been fully respected despite the 2–0 start.\n\nThat gives us another candidate NCAA signal class:\n\n> **Program Reputation Lag** — market price remains partially anchored to historical program strength after current evidence has deteriorated.\n\nAnd I’d split one piece of your statement carefully. “Clemson has given up on that coach” is not something I’d enter as FACT without direct evidence from players, staff behavior, effort metrics, or credible reporting. What we *can* capture is:\n\n**DON DELTA CANDIDATE:** perceived loss of organizational buy-in / coach-cycle deterioration.\n\nThen the model has to ask whether that perception can be operationalized through measurable proxies: effort drop-off, explosive plays allowed, tackling deterioration, penalties, transfer behavior, public player comments, fourth-quarter performance, recruiting/retention signals, etc.\n\nThe other thing I like here is the line movement. If Clemson really opened around -9.5 and collapsed toward -3.5, then the market itself was already correcting toward your thesis before kickoff. citeturn860883news5\n\nSo this case helps define a distinction we need in the schema:\n\n**Don sees an edge** ≠ **the market has not seen it.**\n\nWe need both:\n\n**Don Thesis Timestamp**  \nand  \n**Market Correction Since Thesis**\n\nBecause a great read at Clemson -9.5 may be a completely different proposition by Clemson -3.5.\n\nThat is a major architecture point.\n\nSTATUS: PROCEED  \nCONFIDENCE: 99%  \nREASON: UNC–Clemson adds a third prospective Don signal family — **Program Reputation Lag / Coach-Cycle Deterioration** — while also exposing the need to record whether the market already corrected the perceived edge.  \nNEXT GATE: Continue capturing Don reads prospectively against today’s active slate.  \nDON INPUT NEEDED: No.", "text_chars": 2679, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "5c3b32bd-1a4c-45f7-93de-23c399bfade0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789846624.909219, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "35062bf7-c725-4b24-a35d-4bd82d4a2ea9", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789846624.914322, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "27a9eb3e-54fc-42db-8298-7bcb83f117e4", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789846659.9963431, "updated_at": 1789846685.113053, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah. NCAA is easier to do this with. Now if we get it right, yeah. If we don't, big deal. It's not MLB, everything. I gotta analyze the pitching, the lineup, everything. This is easier to talk through.", "text_chars": 202, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "cfd3b05c-cf6d-4dab-964e-f74c8aa65151", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789846662.466935, "updated_at": 1789846683.127392, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "DATE: 2026-09-19  \nSESSION: EC⁸ Edge Crew Quant — NCAA Football Discovery  \nSEAT: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance  \nCURRENT GATE: Methodology Discovery Through Live Slate\n\nExactly. NCAA is a cleaner discovery environment because the **unit of analysis is more stable**.\n\nIn MLB, every game forces us through starter → pitch mix → handedness splits → lineup card → bullpen availability → catcher → park → weather → umpire → recent workload, and one late lineup change can materially alter the entire calculation.\n\nNCAA still has depth, but we can reason through it more coherently at the **team/system level**:\n\n**team quality → QB → trenches → scheme → matchup → continuity → schedule strength → situational state → venue → market.**\n\nAnd the qualitative layer is much easier to surface conversationally: *this team hasn't actually been tested; this loss was misleading; this program is still priced on reputation; this giant spread assumes dominance that hasn't been proven.*\n\nThe key governance point is that today isn't really about whether we go 5–0 or 0–5 on these reads. The value is whether, **before kickoff**, we can repeatedly explain why our fair number diverges from the market and then diagnose afterward whether the reasoning was structurally correct.\n\nThat gives us a much faster loop for building NCAA than MLB.\n\nSTATUS: PROCEED  \nCONFIDENCE: 99%  \nREASON: NCAA provides a lower-friction environment for discovering and formalizing the relationship between baseline quantitative evidence, situational context, market pricing, and Don Evidence.  \nNEXT GATE: Continue prospective slate reads → postgame reconciliation → identify repeatable NCAA variables  \nDON INPUT NEEDED: No", "text_chars": 1697, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f68f3020-8978-4d65-99a7-53fa6983f650", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789846664.5976436, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e73ce0a6-d3e0-45f2-b798-3d2fd300d0cd", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789846664.9116843, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "79072776-1b63-492e-b46f-10e9369508c4", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789846665.445198, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8aa78208-3b86-4b4f-989e-36272d65ccc3", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789