4. Roster / Personnel\n5. Coaching / Scheme\n6. Matchup\n7. Team Form / Current Performance\n8. Schedule / Situational\n9. Venue / Environment\n10. Game-State / Style Profile\n11. Discipline / Execution\n12. Program / Coaching / Historical Continuity\n13. Market State\n\nThese components are NOT yet locked canon.\n\nYour job is to determine what evidence can populate them reliably.\n\nHistorical evidence must be continuity-conditioned.\n\nCurrent-season samples must preserve opponent strength and sample-size uncertainty.\n\n─────────────────────────\nII. REQUIRED DATA ENTITIES\n─────────────────────────\n\nBuild data around these entities:\n\nGAME\nTEAM\nTEAM-SEASON\nTEAM-GAME\nPLAYER\nPLAYER-SEASON\nPLAYER-GAME\nCOACH\nCOACH-TENURE\nROSTER\nDEPTH CHART\nINJURY / AVAILABILITY\nDRIVE\nPLAY\nMARKET SNAPSHOT\nVENUE\nWEATHER\nHISTORICAL MATCHUP\n\nEvery record should carry, wherever applicable:\n\nevent_id\nseason\nweek\nteam_id\nopponent_id\nplayer_id\nsource\nsource_url\nsource_timestamp\nretrieved_timestamp\ndata_as_of\ndefinition / methodology\nconfidence / quality flag\n\nDo not lose provenance during normalization.\n\n────────────────────────────\nIII. TEAM / GAME CORE PROFILE\n────────────────────────────\n\nFor LSU and Ole Miss first, acquire:\n\nidentity\n- school\n- conference\n- ranking\n- record\n- home / away / neutral\n- opponent\n- date\n- kickoff\n- venue\n- surface\n- altitude if material\n\nscoring\n- points per game\n- points allowed per game\n- scoring by quarter\n- first-half scoring\n- second-half scoring\n- red-zone scoring\n- red-zone TD rate\n\npace / volume\n- plays per game\n- possessions / drives\n- seconds per play if available\n- pass rate\n- rush rate\n- neutral-script pass rate if available\n\nefficiency\n- yards per play\n- yards per drive\n- points per drive\n- first downs\n- third-down conversion\n- fourth-down conversion\n- success rate if available\n- EPA/play if available\n- opponent-adjusted efficiency if available\n\nexplosiveness