y is documented\n- run-block grades if source methodology is documented\n- injuries / substitutions\n\n────────────────\nV. DEFENSE DATA\n────────────────\n\nTeam defense:\n\n- yards/play allowed\n- EPA/play allowed\n- success rate allowed\n- rush efficiency allowed\n- pass efficiency allowed\n- explosive runs allowed\n- explosive passes allowed\n- points/drive allowed\n- third-down defense\n- fourth-down defense\n- red-zone defense\n- sacks\n- pressure rate\n- blitz rate\n- tackles for loss\n- havoc rate\n- interceptions\n- forced fumbles\n- missed tackles if available\n\nDEFENSIVE FRONT\n\n- pressure generation\n- sack production\n- run-stop production\n- TFL production\n- interior vs edge production\n- rotation depth\n- snap distribution\n- injuries\n\nLINEBACKERS\n\n- run stops\n- coverage use\n- missed tackles\n- blitz / pressure production\n- snap volume\n- availability\n\nSECONDARY\n\n- completion % allowed\n- yards/attempt allowed\n- explosive passes allowed\n- interceptions\n- pass breakups\n- coverage grades if documented\n- target data if available\n- injuries\n- lineup continuity\n\n──────────────────────\nVI. SPECIAL TEAMS DATA\n──────────────────────\n\nAcquire:\n\n- field-goal kicker\n- FG %\n- distance splits\n- PAT %\n- punt average\n- net punt\n- punt return efficiency\n- kick return efficiency\n- touchback rate\n- kickoff coverage\n- blocked kicks/punts\n- special-teams touchdowns\n- special-teams EPA or efficiency if reliably available\n\n──────────────────────────\nVII. ROSTER / PERSONNEL DATA\n──────────────────────────\n\nNCAA requires explicit roster-change information.\n\nAcquire:\n\n- returning starters\n- returning production\n- returning offensive production\n- returning defensive production\n- returning QB production\n- transfer additions\n- transfer departures\n- impact transfers\n- recruiting profile\n- talent composite if available\n- position-group experience\n- scholarship / depth concerns if reliably sourced\n- preseason projected starters vs current starters\n- current depth chart\n- major injuries\n- suspensions\n- opt-outs / departures\n- true freshmen playing meaningful snaps\n\nBuild a POSITION CONTINUITY profile for:\n\nQB\nRB\nWR/TE\nOL\nDL\nLB\nDB\n\n──────────────────────\nVIII. COACHING / SCHEME\n──────────────────────\n\nAcquire structured coaching records:\n\n- head coach\n- offensive coordinator\n- defensive coordinator\n- tenure\n- prior position\n- previous team\n- system continuity\n- coordinator changes\n- play-caller\n- defensive play-caller if known\n\nFor scheme, acquire or derive evidence for:\n\nOFFENSE\n- personnel tendencies\n- tempo\n- run/pass tendency\n- RPO usage\n- QB designed-run usage\n- play-action usage\n- motion\n- formation tendencies\n- explosive-play philosophy\n\nDEFENSE\n- front structure\n- man / zone tendencies\n- blitz rate\n- pressure philosophy\n- box-count tendencies\n- explosive-play prevention philosophy\n\nDo not invent scheme classifications where evidence is unavailable.\n\n──────────────────────────────────\nIX. CURRENT FORM / OPPONENT ADJUSTMENT\n──────────────────────────────────\n\nThis is CRITICAL.\n\nFor every current-season game:\n\n- opponent\n- opponent strength\n- score\n- location\n- team yards/play\n- opponent yards/play\n- success rate if available\n- EPA if available\n- turnovers\n- scoring opportunities\n- explosive plays\n- sacks / pressures\n- garbage-time flag if possible\n\nWe must NOT treat:\n\nperformance vs Charlotte\n=\nperformance vs Clemson\n\nas equivalent evidence.\n\nReturn:\n\nRAW PERFORMANCE\nOPPONENT QUALITY\nADJUSTED / CONTEXTUALIZED PERFORMANCE where a defensible method/source exists\n\nIf no reliable opponent-adjustment methodology exists, provide the raw inputs and mark adjustment UNKNOWN.\n\n────────────────────────\nX. LOSS / WIN QUALITY DATA\n────────────────────────\n\nWe are testing a specific NCAA concept:\n\nFINAL SCORE != QUALITY OF PERFORMANCE.\n\nAcquire enough evidence to determine whether a result